<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Constantinople (1832)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1832">1832</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Constantinople was signed in July 1832 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, completing the recognition of the independent Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. It fixed Greece's northern frontier on a line from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambracian-gulf">Gulf of Arta</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagasetic-gulf">Gulf of Volos</a>, and the Ottomans received financial compensation for the lands lost. It followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-conference-of-1832">London Conference of 1832</a>, which chose Otto of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> as king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-constantinople-1832.jpg" alt="Treaty of Constantinople (1832)" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: en:User:Adam Carr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Territorial_Expansion_of_Greece_from_1832%E2%80%931947.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
